1
00:01:13,607 --> 00:01:16,668
There's a club back here? - Yep.

2
00:01:17,311 --> 00:01:20,110
- That's it? We're going in there?
- Yep.

3
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:21,748
You gotta be kidding.

4
00:01:23,183 --> 00:01:24,242
No, I'm not.

5
00:01:24,418 --> 00:01:26,910
What's the matter with you?
You've been doing that all night.

6
00:01:27,087 --> 00:01:29,181
- Hay fever.
- Take something.

7
00:01:29,356 --> 00:01:32,053
I did. It just
didn't kick in yet.

8
00:01:34,828 --> 00:01:36,660
Here we go. Come on.

9
00:01:40,901 --> 00:01:42,529
Excuse me.

10
00:01:48,408 --> 00:01:50,434
What is this, some
kind of speakeasy?

11
00:01:50,611 --> 00:01:53,911
It's the exact replica of one
that was here 65 years ago.

12
00:01:54,081 --> 00:01:56,380
Doesn't it just take
you back in time?

13
00:01:56,550 --> 00:01:58,519
Gangsters. Bootleg whiskey.

14
00:01:58,685 --> 00:02:00,779
The Charleston. Jazz.

15
00:02:01,188 --> 00:02:03,214
- There's Cliff.
- He's with a girl.

16
00:02:03,390 --> 00:02:05,825
He's nuttier than a fruitcake.

17
00:02:05,993 --> 00:02:07,791
Hi. CLIFF: Oh, Leanne.

18
00:02:07,961 --> 00:02:09,589
Come here.

19
00:02:09,763 --> 00:02:11,823
- Uh, Leanne Mclntyre. Ben Matlock.
- Hi.

20
00:02:11,999 --> 00:02:13,126
- Darlene Kellogg.
- Hi.

21
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:14,791
- Hello.
- Dad, you remember Darlene.

22
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:16,061
Nice meeting you.

23
00:02:16,236 --> 00:02:18,102
- Happy birthday.
- Oh, thank you.

24
00:02:18,271 --> 00:02:20,672
Oh, thank you very much, heh.

25
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:25,707
Well, do either one of
you have a cigarette?

26
00:02:25,879 --> 00:02:26,903
- No.
- No.

27
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:29,675
Well, I'm trying to quit.

28
00:02:29,850 --> 00:02:32,115
- Why do you want a cigarette?
- I don't wanna light it.

29
00:02:32,285 --> 00:02:34,525
I just... You know, I need
something to do with my hands.

30
00:02:35,222 --> 00:02:36,588
Do you wanna dance?

31
00:02:36,757 --> 00:02:38,487
My hands, Cliff, not my feet.

32
00:02:38,659 --> 00:02:41,595
Oh. Um, you know, we
could go over and dance

33
00:02:41,762 --> 00:02:43,196
next to the smoking section.

34
00:02:43,363 --> 00:02:45,363
You could get a whole
lungful of second-hand smoke.

35
00:02:45,532 --> 00:02:46,591
Okay.

36
00:02:46,767 --> 00:02:48,736
Excuse us, heh.

37
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:56,639
That boy sure knows how
to pick them, doesn't he?

38
00:02:59,579 --> 00:03:01,707
Are we keeping you up?

39
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:06,720
Can I get you folks
something to drink?

40
00:03:08,121 --> 00:03:09,214
Oh.

41
00:03:09,556 --> 00:03:11,115
I know what you should have.

42
00:03:11,291 --> 00:03:13,419
- Uh, what would that be?
- One of our specials.

43
00:03:13,593 --> 00:03:14,891
Royal English Gin.

44
00:03:15,062 --> 00:03:17,725
Fresh grapefruit
juice. It's pink.

45
00:03:17,898 --> 00:03:19,992
It'll set off those
beautiful eyes you have.

46
00:03:20,634 --> 00:03:21,727
I'll have a Chardonnay.

47
00:03:21,902 --> 00:03:23,302
Wild Turkey on the rocks.

48
00:03:23,470 --> 00:03:25,234
I know what I want.

49
00:03:25,405 --> 00:03:28,933
I'm sorry, sir. I'm afraid I'm not allowed
to serve anyone in your condition.

50
00:03:29,109 --> 00:03:30,475
I'm not drunk.

51
00:03:30,644 --> 00:03:33,739
I just took this pill
for hay fever. I...

52
00:03:33,914 --> 00:03:36,247
Leanne told... I
told you, Leanne.

53
00:03:36,416 --> 00:03:37,543
He'll have cup of coffee.

54
00:03:37,718 --> 00:03:40,153
Coming right up, Leanne.

55
00:03:42,789 --> 00:03:44,121
Oh, boy.

56
00:03:46,860 --> 00:03:52,829
<i>It's raining all the
time</i> I'm going home.

57
00:03:52,999 --> 00:03:54,490
You hate my singing that much?

58
00:03:54,668 --> 00:03:56,193
Oh, no, Billy, it's...

59
00:03:56,536 --> 00:03:59,938
- I'll take a taxi.
- Oh, come on. Don't go.

60
00:04:00,107 --> 00:04:01,939
No, it's not gonna work, Leanne.

61
00:04:02,109 --> 00:04:04,169
I'm miserable.

62
00:04:04,344 --> 00:04:08,372
Tell Cliff I'm sorry, and
look out for that waiter.

63
00:04:08,682 --> 00:04:10,947
He's too slick by half.

64
00:04:11,118 --> 00:04:13,952
Oh, don't worry, Ben.
I'll look after her, heh.

65
00:04:14,121 --> 00:04:15,646
In fact, you wanna dance?

66
00:04:15,822 --> 00:04:17,051
Sure.

67
00:04:17,224 --> 00:04:19,659
- Are you sure you're gonna be okay?
- I'll be fine.

68
00:04:19,826 --> 00:04:23,092
Back in my days in Mount Harlan,
I was pretty much a dancing fool.

69
00:04:24,698 --> 00:04:27,167
You got that half right.

70
00:04:29,369 --> 00:04:30,769
Come on.

71
00:05:25,859 --> 00:05:33,859
<i>Don't know why There's
no sun up in the sky</i>

72
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:36,295
<i>Stormy weather</i>

73
00:05:38,905 --> 00:05:44,970
<i>Since my man
and I ain't together</i>

74
00:05:47,047 --> 00:05:55,047
<i>Keeps raining all the
time</i> DARLENE: Cigars?

75
00:05:55,422 --> 00:05:56,481
Cigarettes?

76
00:05:56,656 --> 00:05:58,352
Cigarillos?

77
00:05:58,525 --> 00:06:01,984
Cigars? Cigarettes?

78
00:06:02,162 --> 00:06:03,960
Cigarillos?

79
00:06:04,130 --> 00:06:07,328
What's the matter with you.

80
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,230
You should ask her out.

81
00:06:09,402 --> 00:06:10,734
I just might do that, boss.

82
00:06:12,939 --> 00:06:14,202
Hello, Ben.

83
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:17,833
Mm. Hello, Billy.

84
00:06:18,011 --> 00:06:20,242
I'll tell you the truth.

85
00:06:20,413 --> 00:06:23,212
Leanne sings like an angel.

86
00:06:23,383 --> 00:06:25,909
Sings like one
and acts like one.

87
00:06:26,086 --> 00:06:28,248
Heck, Ben, she is one.

88
00:06:28,421 --> 00:06:29,855
That's why I
married her, ha, ha.

89
00:06:30,023 --> 00:06:32,117
You're really good.

90
00:06:32,292 --> 00:06:40,292
<i>Keeps raining all the time</i>

91
00:06:52,145 --> 00:06:54,671
Thank you. MAN 1: Yeah!

92
00:06:55,015 --> 00:06:57,678
- Yeah!
- We want more!

93
00:06:58,018 --> 00:07:00,351
Yeah! MAN 3: All right!

94
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:01,988
- Come on!
- Well done.

95
00:07:04,357 --> 00:07:06,349
Ooh.

96
00:07:08,595 --> 00:07:10,530
- Hi, Cliff. Hello, Benjamin.
- Hi.

97
00:07:10,697 --> 00:07:12,723
- Hi.
- How are you?

98
00:07:12,899 --> 00:07:14,231
I'm great.

99
00:07:14,401 --> 00:07:16,597
- So how did I sound?
- You were swell.

100
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:18,033
- Oh.
- Like always.

101
00:07:18,204 --> 00:07:19,832
- Oh.
- Goes for you too, Slick.

102
00:07:20,006 --> 00:07:21,702
Ah, Leanne makes
us all sound good.

103
00:07:23,076 --> 00:07:25,545
How about a drink, everybody?
On the house. What it will be?

104
00:07:25,712 --> 00:07:27,232
Uh, scotch and soda.
- You got it.

105
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:28,609
I'll have one of my specials.

106
00:07:28,782 --> 00:07:31,752
Oh, Ms. Lewis?

107
00:07:31,918 --> 00:07:35,286
I'm always interested
in new libations.

108
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:37,583
What is your special?

109
00:07:37,757 --> 00:07:41,956
A lot of fresh pink
grapefruit juice

110
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:46,463
and just a splash
of Royal English Gin.

111
00:07:46,633 --> 00:07:49,034
Mm. That sounds smooth.

112
00:07:49,369 --> 00:07:51,804
Young gentleman,
I'll have one of those

113
00:07:52,572 --> 00:07:57,237
only reverse the proportions.

114
00:07:57,410 --> 00:08:01,040
A little bit of grapefruit
juice and a lot of gin.

115
00:08:01,214 --> 00:08:04,616
Actually, boss, maybe we
should go back to the office.

116
00:08:04,784 --> 00:08:06,064
Ah. We gotta get that paperwork.

117
00:08:06,219 --> 00:08:08,259
Get it out for Mr. Lewis
first thing in the morning.

118
00:08:08,288 --> 00:08:10,189
One for the road doesn't hurt.

119
00:08:10,357 --> 00:08:12,383
Come on, boss. MATLOCK: Cliff.

120
00:08:12,559 --> 00:08:15,154
A little toddy won't harm me.

121
00:08:15,328 --> 00:08:16,694
Okay.

122
00:08:26,639 --> 00:08:29,871
Smooth.

123
00:08:30,043 --> 00:08:32,603
Let's go, boss.
Come on. Come on.

124
00:08:32,779 --> 00:08:35,146
Good night, everyone.

125
00:08:35,315 --> 00:08:36,442
Good night, everybody.

126
00:08:36,616 --> 00:08:37,777
- Good night.
- Good night.

127
00:08:37,951 --> 00:08:40,978
- Good night.
- Good night. Good night, everyone.

128
00:08:46,993 --> 00:08:48,552
Did you tell him?

129
00:08:48,728 --> 00:08:50,890
What did you say?

130
00:08:58,471 --> 00:09:00,702
I said, did you tell him?

131
00:09:00,874 --> 00:09:03,105
No, not yet.

132
00:09:03,576 --> 00:09:05,943
Why not? What
are you waiting for?

133
00:09:08,114 --> 00:09:10,242
The right time.

134
00:09:10,417 --> 00:09:13,285
Why don't you just be patient?

135
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:15,686
One more week, Leanne.

136
00:09:15,855 --> 00:09:18,415
If you don't tell him you
want a divorce by then, I will.

137
00:09:18,591 --> 00:09:20,253
You hear me?

138
00:09:22,228 --> 00:09:23,787
No.

139
00:09:24,364 --> 00:09:27,892
Why don't you come a little
closer and tell me again?

140
00:10:11,411 --> 00:10:13,107
That was good. - All right.

141
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:15,510
You gotta work on that bit.
- Okay.

142
00:10:15,682 --> 00:10:17,674
I, um, I have to talk to you.

143
00:10:17,851 --> 00:10:19,843
- When, now?
- Right over here.

144
00:10:20,019 --> 00:10:21,851
What's the matter?

145
00:10:24,090 --> 00:10:25,854
I'm gonna tell him.

146
00:10:26,025 --> 00:10:28,119
- Tonight.
- Well, that's great.

147
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:30,991
- But why do you have to...?
- I have to be sure, Slick.

148
00:10:31,164 --> 00:10:32,188
Say you love me.

149
00:10:32,665 --> 00:10:34,964
Say it. Please.

150
00:10:35,135 --> 00:10:36,967
Oh, baby.

151
00:10:37,137 --> 00:10:39,106
You know I do.

152
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:44,036
I told you to keep
your hands off of me.

153
00:10:49,082 --> 00:10:51,074
Get your stuff and clear
out here. You're through.

154
00:11:02,195 --> 00:11:04,960
Oh, he's been
after me for months.

155
00:11:05,131 --> 00:11:07,999
Touching me, saying things.

156
00:11:09,602 --> 00:11:11,070
I didn't know what to do.

157
00:11:11,237 --> 00:11:13,263
Why didn't you tell me?

158
00:11:13,439 --> 00:11:15,135
I just didn't wanna upset you.

159
00:11:15,308 --> 00:11:16,936
Yeah. It's okay.

160
00:11:17,110 --> 00:11:20,205
He won't bother you
anymore. I promise.

161
00:11:31,157 --> 00:11:32,955
Slick.

162
00:11:33,493 --> 00:11:35,519
Baby.

163
00:11:40,133 --> 00:11:41,692
Ah. Oh.

164
00:11:43,136 --> 00:11:44,968
I just had to do
that. I'm so sorry.

165
00:11:45,138 --> 00:11:47,630
You're sorry? Hell,
I'm out of a job.

166
00:11:47,807 --> 00:11:50,038
Oh, Slick.

167
00:11:50,910 --> 00:11:53,277
Don't you see?

168
00:11:53,446 --> 00:11:57,213
If Billy had thought for a second
there was anything between us,

169
00:11:57,383 --> 00:12:00,012
he would have thrown me out too,

170
00:12:00,186 --> 00:12:03,588
and we both would have
wound up in the poor house.

171
00:12:03,756 --> 00:12:06,225
He would have made sure of that.

172
00:12:06,926 --> 00:12:08,724
- Yeah.
- Mm.

173
00:12:09,362 --> 00:12:11,558
- Yeah, you're right, baby.
- Mm.

174
00:12:11,831 --> 00:12:14,323
What you did was smart.

175
00:12:14,801 --> 00:12:16,599
Yeah. Real smart.

176
00:12:19,172 --> 00:12:20,606
Oh, I gotta go.

177
00:12:22,008 --> 00:12:25,069
I just wanted to make
sure you were all right.

178
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:41,884
Ah. So I'll see you
tomorrow at 2:45?

179
00:12:42,061 --> 00:12:43,654
Oh, I'll be here.

180
00:12:45,031 --> 00:12:48,092
Well, I intend to
make this up to you.

181
00:12:55,108 --> 00:12:58,203
<i>I'm with you always</i>

182
00:12:58,378 --> 00:13:02,748
<i>I'm with you rain or shine</i>

183
00:13:05,718 --> 00:13:13,421
<i>I'm with you rain or shine</i>

184
00:13:19,232 --> 00:13:20,530
All right.

185
00:13:22,201 --> 00:13:23,692
Sounded okay without the sax?

186
00:13:23,870 --> 00:13:25,304
It sounded great, sweetheart.

187
00:13:25,471 --> 00:13:27,872
Mm. I gotta go.

188
00:13:28,041 --> 00:13:32,240
Your mom's mineral bath is
at 2:30. Wanna come with me?

189
00:13:32,412 --> 00:13:34,847
I can't. I got a meeting at 3.

190
00:13:35,014 --> 00:13:37,609
Okay. I'll see you later.

191
00:14:18,157 --> 00:14:20,023
<i>Dr. Thomas. Dr. Thomas.</i>

192
00:14:20,193 --> 00:14:23,493
<i>Dr. Thomas, please
talk to the main desk.</i>

193
00:14:23,663 --> 00:14:25,825
- Hello, Mrs. Lewis.
- Oh, hello.

194
00:14:25,998 --> 00:14:27,364
How are we doing today?

195
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:29,661
- I'm...
- Oh, not very well, I'm afraid.

196
00:14:29,836 --> 00:14:32,499
She aches all over,
especially her hands.

197
00:14:32,672 --> 00:14:34,664
Well, let's see what
we can do about that.

198
00:14:34,841 --> 00:14:35,968
Oh, yes.

199
00:14:36,142 --> 00:14:37,633
Now, it's gonna take
us about an hour.

200
00:14:37,810 --> 00:14:39,574
That's all right. I have a book.

201
00:14:40,213 --> 00:14:42,375
- Goodbye, Mother Lewis.
- Oh, bye-bye.

202
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:44,380
I'll be right here.

203
00:15:03,403 --> 00:15:04,996
Hi.

204
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:11,901
Oh, you got a haircut.

205
00:15:12,078 --> 00:15:13,478
Yeah. You like it?

206
00:15:13,646 --> 00:15:14,944
I love it.

207
00:15:15,114 --> 00:15:17,640
Um, how about if
we have a drink first?

208
00:15:17,817 --> 00:15:19,809
- Coming right up.
- Heh.

209
00:15:43,709 --> 00:15:44,733
Slick, honey?

210
00:15:44,911 --> 00:15:46,072
Yeah?

211
00:15:49,382 --> 00:15:51,476
Sorry, baby.

212
00:16:47,006 --> 00:16:48,030
Slick.

213
00:17:01,621 --> 00:17:04,682
Oh, hello. Is this the police?

214
00:17:41,093 --> 00:17:43,494
He didn't do it, Ben.

215
00:17:44,463 --> 00:17:47,456
I mean, he may get
mad every now and then,

216
00:17:47,633 --> 00:17:50,626
but he never stays mad.

217
00:17:50,803 --> 00:17:53,272
He didn't kill Slick.

218
00:17:53,439 --> 00:17:55,169
Will you take his case?

219
00:17:55,374 --> 00:17:56,899
Please?

220
00:17:57,276 --> 00:18:01,509
I'm sorry, Mrs. Lewis, I can't.

221
00:18:01,681 --> 00:18:02,705
But why?

222
00:18:02,882 --> 00:18:04,783
I have trials coming up,

223
00:18:04,951 --> 00:18:07,511
writs to write,
hearings, depositions.

224
00:18:07,687 --> 00:18:10,714
My calendar is packed full.

225
00:18:13,626 --> 00:18:16,892
But you've just
got to take his case.

226
00:18:18,698 --> 00:18:20,496
You've just got to.

227
00:18:20,666 --> 00:18:23,727
Mrs. Lewis, there are lots
of good lawyers in town.

228
00:18:23,903 --> 00:18:25,667
Let me write down a few names.

229
00:18:25,838 --> 00:18:27,329
No.

230
00:18:32,612 --> 00:18:36,014
He doesn't want
just any old lawyer.

231
00:18:38,017 --> 00:18:39,815
Mrs. Lewis,

232
00:18:39,986 --> 00:18:42,080
would you excuse
us for one minute?

233
00:18:42,254 --> 00:18:44,018
Certainly.

234
00:18:44,624 --> 00:18:46,388
Shall I wait in the hall?

235
00:18:46,559 --> 00:18:49,324
That would be fine. - Oh.

236
00:18:55,735 --> 00:18:57,101
Thank you.

237
00:18:57,269 --> 00:18:58,293
You're welcome.

238
00:18:59,338 --> 00:19:02,035
Boss, what are
you talking about?

239
00:19:02,208 --> 00:19:05,178
You don't have
any writs to write.

240
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:10,440
Billy's life is in danger.

241
00:19:10,616 --> 00:19:14,519
He needs a competent lawyer,
and that sure as hell ain't me.

242
00:19:14,687 --> 00:19:17,714
Yes, it is. You can do it.

243
00:19:19,925 --> 00:19:21,052
I don't know.

244
00:19:22,662 --> 00:19:26,394
You still got what it takes to be the
best defense lawyer in the country, boss.

245
00:19:26,565 --> 00:19:27,726
I know you do.

246
00:19:28,901 --> 00:19:32,605
Deep down inside, I
think you know it too.

247
00:19:36,709 --> 00:19:38,439
The shot those people heard came

248
00:19:38,611 --> 00:19:41,274
from outside the
rooming house, not inside.

249
00:19:41,447 --> 00:19:43,473
I heard it too.

250
00:19:44,483 --> 00:19:47,009
And you didn't fire the pistol?

251
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:49,883
I found the gun by the body.

252
00:19:50,056 --> 00:19:55,085
When I realized it was
mine, I got scared and ran.

253
00:19:55,895 --> 00:19:59,332
What were you doing at
Slick's apartment to start with?

254
00:19:59,498 --> 00:20:03,230
He left me a note asking
me to come over at 3

255
00:20:03,402 --> 00:20:06,463
so he could explain
about him and Leanne.

256
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:10,604
- Could I see it?
- See what?

257
00:20:10,776 --> 00:20:11,869
The note.

258
00:20:12,044 --> 00:20:13,512
I don't have it.

259
00:20:13,679 --> 00:20:15,511
I could've sworn I
left it in my office,

260
00:20:15,681 --> 00:20:18,344
but the police said
they couldn't find it.

261
00:20:20,519 --> 00:20:21,919
Doesn't look good, does it?

262
00:20:22,088 --> 00:20:23,112
Hmm.

263
00:20:24,256 --> 00:20:25,815
Uh...

264
00:20:26,759 --> 00:20:29,627
At least you're on my side, Ben.

265
00:20:32,264 --> 00:20:35,291
Can't tell you how
good that makes me feel.

266
00:20:50,382 --> 00:20:52,442
Hey, look at this.

267
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:55,949
Looks like some of
the clothes are missing.

268
00:20:56,122 --> 00:20:59,183
Mm. Mm-hm.

269
00:21:20,079 --> 00:21:21,945
Something's missing.

270
00:21:22,114 --> 00:21:23,810
What did you say?

271
00:21:25,151 --> 00:21:26,881
Nothing.

272
00:21:31,924 --> 00:21:34,985
I wonder what happened
to this other green pillow.

273
00:21:37,830 --> 00:21:38,923
What are you doing, boss?

274
00:21:39,098 --> 00:21:41,658
I got cobwebs in my
head. I need to flush it out.

275
00:21:41,834 --> 00:21:42,961
- No, you don't.
- Yes, I do.

276
00:21:43,135 --> 00:21:46,435
No, you don't. No,
you don't. No, you don't.

277
00:21:52,278 --> 00:21:53,837
Oh, I'll be damned.

278
00:21:54,013 --> 00:21:55,242
What's the matter?

279
00:21:55,414 --> 00:21:57,781
Well, this is gin.

280
00:21:58,284 --> 00:22:00,446
And grapefruit juice.

281
00:22:01,654 --> 00:22:03,680
Oh, my gosh.

282
00:22:13,532 --> 00:22:15,626
Oh, hi. Come on in.

283
00:22:15,801 --> 00:22:16,962
Hello, Ben.

284
00:22:17,136 --> 00:22:18,729
Sorry it took me so long.

285
00:22:18,904 --> 00:22:20,805
I had a terrible time
finding this place.

286
00:22:20,973 --> 00:22:22,965
Well, thanks for coming.

287
00:22:23,475 --> 00:22:25,376
Well, have a seat.

288
00:22:34,386 --> 00:22:38,619
Well, we're making progress.

289
00:22:40,926 --> 00:22:44,954
Cliff and I think Slick
had a roommate.

290
00:22:45,130 --> 00:22:47,725
There's a big empty
space in the closet.

291
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:51,735
Like somebody took a bunch
of clothes out of there recently.

292
00:22:51,904 --> 00:22:53,372
Hmm.

293
00:22:54,073 --> 00:22:58,306
Well, maybe Slick took some
of his things to the laundry.

294
00:22:58,477 --> 00:23:01,709
Well, that's possible.
That's entirely possible.

295
00:23:01,881 --> 00:23:06,444
Uh, Cliff is, uh, looking
into that as we speak.

296
00:23:10,155 --> 00:23:13,387
And there's a bunch of stuff

297
00:23:13,559 --> 00:23:17,394
missing out of the medicine
chest in the bathroom.

298
00:23:17,563 --> 00:23:21,933
And knowing how Slick was
fond of female companionship

299
00:23:23,068 --> 00:23:28,735
leads me to believe that
his roommate was a woman.

300
00:23:29,508 --> 00:23:32,137
That wouldn't surprise me, Ben.

301
00:23:33,078 --> 00:23:35,980
But tell me, why
is that important?

302
00:23:36,315 --> 00:23:38,079
She could be the killer.

303
00:23:38,417 --> 00:23:41,683
The police got two phone
calls about the gunshots,

304
00:23:41,954 --> 00:23:43,889
both women.

305
00:23:44,056 --> 00:23:48,255
One was a neighbor
lady and the other, I think,

306
00:23:48,427 --> 00:23:53,092
the woman who wouldn't
identify herself, is the killer.

307
00:23:53,799 --> 00:23:58,533
Called the police to get
here just in time to catch Billy.

308
00:23:59,972 --> 00:24:01,531
And...

309
00:24:02,341 --> 00:24:03,866
What?

310
00:24:07,079 --> 00:24:13,610
The only thing Slick was wearing
when he was shot was a bathrobe.

311
00:24:13,786 --> 00:24:16,654
I mean, the only thing.

312
00:24:18,757 --> 00:24:23,718
And that leads me to believe
that he was expecting somebody

313
00:24:23,896 --> 00:24:26,798
of the female persuasion.

314
00:24:27,166 --> 00:24:29,761
Well, everything's going good.

315
00:24:29,935 --> 00:24:32,666
I feel like celebrating.
A little party.

316
00:24:32,838 --> 00:24:34,136
How about a drink?

317
00:24:34,306 --> 00:24:39,404
I found the mixings to your
favorite here in Slick's place.

318
00:24:45,684 --> 00:24:48,779
You know, Slick had one
of mine at the club one night.

319
00:24:48,954 --> 00:24:50,047
Uh-huh.

320
00:24:50,222 --> 00:24:53,215
I, um, guess he got hooked.

321
00:24:53,392 --> 00:24:54,451
Yeah, heh.

322
00:24:54,626 --> 00:24:57,391
Well, I squeezed some
fresh grapefruit juice

323
00:24:57,563 --> 00:24:59,794
while I was
waiting for you, so...

324
00:24:59,965 --> 00:25:01,365
- Here. Oh.
- Aah!

325
00:25:01,967 --> 00:25:03,731
- Oh, I'm...
- Oh, look what you've done.

326
00:25:03,902 --> 00:25:05,632
Oh, I'm so sorry.

327
00:25:05,804 --> 00:25:09,536
This is pure silk. You've
probably just ruined it. Oh.

328
00:25:09,708 --> 00:25:14,146
Now, how did you know that
dish towel was in that drawer?

329
00:25:19,084 --> 00:25:23,283
I got a few tricks up
my sleeve still, don't I?

330
00:25:26,392 --> 00:25:28,054
All right.

331
00:25:29,294 --> 00:25:31,160
It's true.

332
00:25:33,399 --> 00:25:35,664
We had an affair.

333
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:40,464
Oh, Ben.

334
00:25:41,507 --> 00:25:43,476
It was just awful.

335
00:25:46,211 --> 00:25:48,908
He just wouldn't
leave me alone, Ben.

336
00:25:49,081 --> 00:25:54,952
He hounded me day
and night, night and day.

337
00:25:56,789 --> 00:25:59,759
Until I finally gave in to him.

338
00:25:59,925 --> 00:26:01,689
Oh.

339
00:26:07,733 --> 00:26:09,429
Oh, Ben.

340
00:26:11,970 --> 00:26:14,906
It only lasted a
couple of weeks.

341
00:26:16,008 --> 00:26:18,341
As a matter of fact,

342
00:26:19,111 --> 00:26:24,482
that fight we had in the
club when Billy slugged Slick,

343
00:26:25,250 --> 00:26:28,379
I was breaking it off
with him, but he just...

344
00:26:28,654 --> 00:26:30,919
He wouldn't accept it.

345
00:26:32,091 --> 00:26:35,584
So that stuff that's
gone is yours?

346
00:26:37,096 --> 00:26:38,758
Yes.

347
00:26:39,898 --> 00:26:46,134
I came over here that
night to get my things.

348
00:26:49,208 --> 00:26:51,905
I never wanted to see him again.

349
00:26:57,449 --> 00:26:59,384
And I didn't.

350
00:27:05,824 --> 00:27:09,386
I didn't have anything to
do with the murder, Ben.

351
00:27:10,162 --> 00:27:11,687
In fact,

352
00:27:11,864 --> 00:27:16,598
I was at the clinic with Billy's
mother when it happened.

353
00:27:17,469 --> 00:27:20,200
I want you to check that out.

354
00:27:23,442 --> 00:27:25,536
Oh, Ben.

355
00:27:34,853 --> 00:27:36,412
Bye.

356
00:27:58,143 --> 00:27:59,736
Cheer up, Billy.

357
00:27:59,912 --> 00:28:03,508
Your ace lawyer is
here to save the day.

358
00:28:16,161 --> 00:28:17,857
How you doing?

359
00:28:18,397 --> 00:28:20,127
I'm okay.

360
00:28:23,268 --> 00:28:27,103
Did you tell anybody you was
going over to Slick's that afternoon?

361
00:28:27,272 --> 00:28:28,740
No.

362
00:28:31,610 --> 00:28:33,704
Did you tell Leanne?

363
00:28:34,313 --> 00:28:37,681
She already thinks
I'm too much of a softie.

364
00:28:38,050 --> 00:28:42,317
I just told her I
had a meeting at 3.

365
00:28:45,824 --> 00:28:48,191
- Billy...
- I already know about her and Slick,

366
00:28:48,360 --> 00:28:49,760
if that's what
you're getting at.

367
00:28:51,263 --> 00:28:54,199
- You do?
- She was just here.

368
00:28:55,467 --> 00:28:57,095
Told me everything.

369
00:28:57,269 --> 00:29:00,034
Poor kid. She felt
terrible about it.

370
00:29:00,572 --> 00:29:03,303
Cried the whole time, heh.

371
00:29:03,475 --> 00:29:05,808
About broke my heart.

372
00:29:08,413 --> 00:29:11,542
You're not mad?

373
00:29:12,050 --> 00:29:14,246
Come on, Ben.

374
00:29:14,419 --> 00:29:16,718
I know I'm too old for her.

375
00:29:16,888 --> 00:29:20,723
I'm not handsome or debonair.

376
00:29:21,660 --> 00:29:23,390
Slick was able to seduce her.

377
00:29:23,562 --> 00:29:26,191
It's my fault, not hers.

378
00:29:26,431 --> 00:29:29,595
So she had a moment of weakness.

379
00:29:30,535 --> 00:29:34,802
I figure, for all the joy she's given me
in the three years we've been married,

380
00:29:34,973 --> 00:29:38,569
heh, I'm still way ahead.

381
00:29:40,245 --> 00:29:42,840
- What if she's lying?
- Lying?

382
00:29:43,348 --> 00:29:45,249
Leanne loved me, Ben.

383
00:29:45,417 --> 00:29:47,613
I saw her push Slick
away with my own eyes.

384
00:29:47,786 --> 00:29:50,085
She was rejecting him for me.

385
00:29:50,255 --> 00:29:51,689
That woman's a saint.

386
00:29:51,857 --> 00:29:55,385
In fact, hiring you to
defend me was her idea.

387
00:29:55,761 --> 00:29:59,493
I thought it'd be too much for
you, but she went to bat for you.

388
00:29:59,665 --> 00:30:02,760
Said we ought to give you
a chance to redeem yourself.

389
00:30:02,934 --> 00:30:06,769
Now here you are
running her down.

390
00:30:07,005 --> 00:30:09,304
You ought to be ashamed.

391
00:30:10,142 --> 00:30:13,374
Ahem, Billy, I was just...

392
00:30:13,545 --> 00:30:16,572
It must be the sauce, Ben.

393
00:30:17,249 --> 00:30:19,218
Maybe, uh...

394
00:30:19,851 --> 00:30:24,585
Maybe you should think
about cutting back for a while.

395
00:30:34,199 --> 00:30:35,929
Here, let me take
your briefcase.

396
00:30:36,101 --> 00:30:37,433
Hmm.

397
00:30:38,904 --> 00:30:41,100
- Have a seat.
- Oh, thank you.

398
00:30:44,076 --> 00:30:46,204
Would you like a drink?

399
00:30:47,646 --> 00:30:51,344
Is that why you asked me to stop
by, so you could offer me a drink?

400
00:30:51,516 --> 00:30:54,145
Just trying to be polite, Ben.

401
00:30:55,687 --> 00:30:58,816
I'm gonna stay sober
until after Billy's trial.

402
00:30:58,990 --> 00:31:03,121
Oh. Well, good for you.

403
00:31:03,762 --> 00:31:05,355
Mind if I indulge?

404
00:31:05,530 --> 00:31:07,556
No. Help yourself.

405
00:31:09,701 --> 00:31:12,466
I've switched to Scotch.

406
00:31:13,205 --> 00:31:16,607
I just got so tired
of grapefruit juice.

407
00:31:18,643 --> 00:31:21,875
Scotch is your
favorite, as I recall.

408
00:31:26,685 --> 00:31:28,210
Mmm, tsk.

409
00:31:30,455 --> 00:31:32,481
Sure I can't tempt you?

410
00:31:32,657 --> 00:31:35,024
Well, I could use something.

411
00:31:35,193 --> 00:31:38,789
- How about some iced tea?
- No, it's fine.

412
00:31:38,964 --> 00:31:42,025
Ben, I'll get
right to the point.

413
00:31:42,200 --> 00:31:44,795
I know you think I had something
to do with Slick's murder.

414
00:31:44,970 --> 00:31:48,702
I wanted to convince
you that that wasn't true

415
00:31:48,874 --> 00:31:52,276
before you made a
fool of yourself in court.

416
00:32:01,186 --> 00:32:03,951
I know you don't believe it.

417
00:32:04,456 --> 00:32:07,688
But the fact is, I love Billy.

418
00:32:08,460 --> 00:32:10,258
Very much.

419
00:32:10,429 --> 00:32:13,263
And I'm gonna be
in court every day.

420
00:32:13,432 --> 00:32:15,128
And I'm gonna hold
his hand every day,

421
00:32:15,300 --> 00:32:17,201
and I'm gonna
whisper in his ear.

422
00:32:17,669 --> 00:32:20,332
And I'm going to let
the jury see firsthand

423
00:32:20,505 --> 00:32:22,736
just how much I love him.

424
00:32:23,909 --> 00:32:25,434
So

425
00:32:28,613 --> 00:32:32,277
To suggest

426
00:32:34,286 --> 00:32:37,654
that I framed Billy,
well, that would be...

427
00:32:38,190 --> 00:32:40,921
That would be pretty
stupid, don't you think?

428
00:32:42,461 --> 00:32:45,795
All I need to get Billy off is
to plant the seed of doubt

429
00:32:45,964 --> 00:32:49,025
in one juror's mind.

430
00:32:49,201 --> 00:32:50,931
And you think you can do that?

431
00:32:51,102 --> 00:32:54,561
Well, I talked to the nurse at the
clinic where you took his mother,

432
00:32:54,739 --> 00:33:00,235
and you were alone in that
waiting room for an hour at least.

433
00:33:00,412 --> 00:33:02,381
That's what you said.

434
00:33:06,952 --> 00:33:08,921
Thank you for the tea.

435
00:33:09,921 --> 00:33:11,583
That's enough.

436
00:33:12,557 --> 00:33:14,253
I'll see you in...

437
00:33:31,376 --> 00:33:33,368
You all right, Ben?

438
00:33:34,446 --> 00:33:36,472
- Where is he?
- Where the heck is he?

439
00:33:36,648 --> 00:33:38,310
All rise.

440
00:33:38,483 --> 00:33:41,385
The Honorable Judge
Caldwell presiding.

441
00:33:41,553 --> 00:33:43,419
Babycakes, I'm so sorry.

442
00:33:43,588 --> 00:33:45,648
Ben Matlock's back at the
club and he's dead drunk.

443
00:33:45,824 --> 00:33:48,664
I tried to keep him from drinking,
but there wasn't anything I could do.

444
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:50,856
Be seated.

445
00:33:51,029 --> 00:33:52,554
Uh...

446
00:33:54,199 --> 00:33:57,658
Uh, Your Honor, um...

447
00:33:58,303 --> 00:34:01,273
Lead counsel has been delayed.

448
00:34:01,673 --> 00:34:03,869
- Request a brief recess?
- How brief?

449
00:34:04,209 --> 00:34:05,677
Oh, about an hour.

450
00:34:05,844 --> 00:34:07,506
Try 20 minutes, counselor.

451
00:34:07,846 --> 00:34:09,246
Right.

452
00:34:15,654 --> 00:34:17,054
Boss, come on, now.

453
00:34:17,222 --> 00:34:18,884
Boss, you said you
were gonna stay sober.

454
00:34:19,057 --> 00:34:20,389
Wake up, boss. Come on.

455
00:34:20,559 --> 00:34:23,051
- Uh... Cliff, what?
- Cliff, what?

456
00:34:23,228 --> 00:34:24,821
Boss, you sound... You're drunk.

457
00:34:24,996 --> 00:34:28,660
How could you do this?
Billy was depending on you.

458
00:34:29,267 --> 00:34:32,260
- Billy.
- Billy.

459
00:34:33,104 --> 00:34:34,538
Billy.

460
00:34:37,742 --> 00:34:39,301
Oh, my God.

461
00:34:39,477 --> 00:34:40,536
Oh, wait a second.

462
00:34:40,712 --> 00:34:42,078
- Where are you going?
- I'm late.

463
00:34:42,247 --> 00:34:43,271
No. Boss.

464
00:34:43,448 --> 00:34:46,043
Now, boss, you're in no
condition to go anywhere, boss.

465
00:34:46,217 --> 00:34:47,480
Now, hold on. Boss.

466
00:34:47,652 --> 00:34:50,247
- Let go of me.
- No, you are in no condition to go.

467
00:34:50,422 --> 00:34:52,448
I said, let go of me.
I've gotta go to court.

468
00:34:55,493 --> 00:34:56,688
Taxi!

469
00:34:59,197 --> 00:35:01,189
Well, in view of the fact

470
00:35:01,366 --> 00:35:05,326
that the defendant now seems
to be without any counsel at all

471
00:35:05,503 --> 00:35:07,199
I hereby order that...

472
00:35:07,372 --> 00:35:09,307
Ben Matlock for the
defense, Your Honor.

473
00:35:09,474 --> 00:35:10,737
Mr. Matlock.

474
00:35:10,909 --> 00:35:14,903
Yeah. Now, if the court
please, a moment with my client.

475
00:35:15,080 --> 00:35:16,776
Mr. Matlock, you
are in contempt.

476
00:35:17,082 --> 00:35:18,550
Yes, sir.

477
00:35:18,717 --> 00:35:20,117
We have to talk.

478
00:35:20,285 --> 00:35:22,311
My, God, Ben, you're loaded.

479
00:35:22,487 --> 00:35:23,716
Bailiff, remove that man.

480
00:35:26,691 --> 00:35:28,683
- You're fired, Ben.
- No, no.

481
00:35:28,860 --> 00:35:31,261
I should never have
hired you in the first place.

482
00:35:31,429 --> 00:35:32,954
Billy, Billy. Billy,
you've got...

483
00:35:33,131 --> 00:35:34,224
You've got to believe me.

484
00:35:34,399 --> 00:35:37,995
Billy, please. You
have to believe me, Billy.

485
00:35:38,703 --> 00:35:40,194
She's... Billy, please.

486
00:35:41,072 --> 00:35:43,803
You have to believe me, Billy.

487
00:36:13,571 --> 00:36:14,766
Wanted to see me, boss?

488
00:36:14,939 --> 00:36:16,100
Ah, Cliff.

489
00:36:17,676 --> 00:36:19,668
You're a nice kid, Cliff.

490
00:36:19,844 --> 00:36:21,676
Smart too.

491
00:36:22,247 --> 00:36:25,945
Too smart to let a loser
like me hold you back.

492
00:36:26,117 --> 00:36:29,053
I'm not quite following
your thinking, boss.

493
00:36:29,421 --> 00:36:33,449
I got a couple friends who are lawyers,
and I told them you're the greatest.

494
00:36:33,625 --> 00:36:37,323
You won't have any
trouble getting a job.

495
00:36:37,829 --> 00:36:40,663
- Who said I was quitting?
- Me.

496
00:36:41,933 --> 00:36:43,026
It's over.

497
00:36:43,201 --> 00:36:44,829
It's done.

498
00:36:45,637 --> 00:36:49,472
If I can't keep up with a
small-town broad like Leanne

499
00:36:49,641 --> 00:36:51,872
it's time to call it a day.

500
00:36:52,043 --> 00:36:55,104
I should have known
she was up to something.

501
00:36:55,847 --> 00:36:59,306
I should have seen that
Mickey coming, but I didn't.

502
00:36:59,484 --> 00:37:01,749
Hell, no.

503
00:37:02,554 --> 00:37:05,353
Boss, you were the best.

504
00:37:07,292 --> 00:37:08,692
Yeah.

505
00:37:10,995 --> 00:37:12,554
Yeah, I was.

506
00:37:12,731 --> 00:37:14,927
I was the best.

507
00:37:15,767 --> 00:37:18,430
I got all the big cases.

508
00:37:18,970 --> 00:37:20,131
I've won them too.

509
00:37:20,972 --> 00:37:22,634
Most of them.

510
00:37:22,807 --> 00:37:24,867
I was really something.

511
00:37:25,477 --> 00:37:27,776
And then one day,
this rich college boy

512
00:37:27,946 --> 00:37:30,848
came in my office
charged with murder.

513
00:37:31,015 --> 00:37:33,712
The state has a strong case.

514
00:37:34,686 --> 00:37:36,279
Mine was stronger.

515
00:37:36,454 --> 00:37:38,753
I got my boy off.

516
00:37:39,224 --> 00:37:41,716
I raised my fee.

517
00:37:45,830 --> 00:37:48,322
And then there
was another murder.

518
00:37:50,635 --> 00:37:53,434
And the state charged
my boy with that one,

519
00:37:53,605 --> 00:37:56,473
and they had an air-tight case.

520
00:37:56,908 --> 00:38:03,310
He confessed to that
murder and the first.

521
00:38:05,817 --> 00:38:09,720
And the papers blamed
me for the second murder.

522
00:38:15,093 --> 00:38:17,460
Called me a monster.

523
00:38:18,596 --> 00:38:21,156
Everybody's entitled
to representation.

524
00:38:21,332 --> 00:38:24,131
Hell, I'm just doing my job.

525
00:38:24,302 --> 00:38:26,237
You were.

526
00:38:28,673 --> 00:38:32,269
It's not up to us to decide
who's innocent or who's guilty.

527
00:38:32,443 --> 00:38:34,207
I know.

528
00:38:34,512 --> 00:38:40,383
That's the foundation of
this religion we call the law.

529
00:38:41,286 --> 00:38:44,551
But somehow...
Somehow, when that...

530
00:38:44,722 --> 00:38:47,886
When that boy confessed, I...

531
00:38:48,593 --> 00:38:50,585
I couldn't believe anymore.

532
00:38:54,399 --> 00:38:56,868
I lost my faith.

533
00:38:57,402 --> 00:38:59,234
But I found this.

534
00:39:01,439 --> 00:39:04,170
You may have lost your faith,
boss, but you still got your talent.

535
00:39:04,342 --> 00:39:05,674
- I know that you do.
- Heh.

536
00:39:05,844 --> 00:39:07,608
Come on, you can't
let her do this to you.

537
00:39:07,779 --> 00:39:09,748
You can't let her
get away with this.

538
00:39:09,914 --> 00:39:16,218
Son, she already has.

539
00:39:17,889 --> 00:39:20,051
- Mm.
- No! No.

540
00:39:20,225 --> 00:39:21,853
No. Come on. Come on.

541
00:39:22,026 --> 00:39:23,790
- No. Come on.
- For what?

542
00:39:23,962 --> 00:39:25,191
- Come on. Just...
- What?

543
00:39:25,363 --> 00:39:27,195
- Watch yourself. Come with me.
- Where?

544
00:39:27,365 --> 00:39:28,890
- We're going somewhere.
- Where?

545
00:39:29,067 --> 00:39:31,400
- You'll see when we get there.
- But you don't realize...

546
00:39:31,569 --> 00:39:34,095
Well, where are you...?

547
00:39:40,678 --> 00:39:43,546
Here's more. Just keep drinking.

548
00:39:47,952 --> 00:39:49,477
If Leanne tripped
herself up anywhere,

549
00:39:49,654 --> 00:39:52,488
she did it right here at
the scene of the crime.

550
00:39:52,657 --> 00:39:54,455
We've been over
this place, Cliff.

551
00:39:54,993 --> 00:39:57,553
Yeah, well, you
were soused then.

552
00:39:57,729 --> 00:39:59,721
Now you're sober.

553
00:40:01,099 --> 00:40:02,795
Kind of.

554
00:40:21,152 --> 00:40:23,280
Something's missing.

555
00:40:24,188 --> 00:40:26,157
Something's missing.

556
00:40:26,958 --> 00:40:30,417
Good Lord, how long has it
been since I combed my hair?

557
00:40:30,595 --> 00:40:32,621
- Heh.
- Oh.

558
00:40:36,968 --> 00:40:39,233
There's no hairbrush.

559
00:40:40,672 --> 00:40:43,005
That's what's missing.

560
00:40:43,708 --> 00:40:45,836
His hairbrush.

561
00:40:48,212 --> 00:40:49,703
Huh.

562
00:41:00,124 --> 00:41:02,150
Excuse me.

563
00:41:02,327 --> 00:41:04,956
- Where's Billy?
- He's over there.

564
00:41:16,274 --> 00:41:19,733
Be seated. Is the
defense ready to proceed?

565
00:41:24,048 --> 00:41:27,109
Your Honor, my client
would like to make a request.

566
00:41:27,285 --> 00:41:28,844
All right.

567
00:41:29,687 --> 00:41:32,350
I'd like to reinstate Ben
Matlock as my lawyer.

568
00:41:33,758 --> 00:41:35,420
So be it.

569
00:41:37,362 --> 00:41:41,663
Defense calls Miss
Leanne Lewis to the stand.

570
00:41:41,833 --> 00:41:44,234
Giving in to Slick like
that was the stupidest thing

571
00:41:44,402 --> 00:41:47,338
I've ever done in
my whole entire life.

572
00:41:47,505 --> 00:41:51,067
But he was so insistent
and overbearing

573
00:41:51,242 --> 00:41:53,143
that it took me a
couple of weeks

574
00:41:53,311 --> 00:41:55,780
to get up the courage
to break it off with him.

575
00:41:56,414 --> 00:41:59,384
That's what we were fighting
about at the club that night.

576
00:41:59,550 --> 00:42:01,485
You told him it was over?

577
00:42:02,253 --> 00:42:05,155
And that night, when I
knew he wouldn't be there,

578
00:42:05,323 --> 00:42:08,316
I went over to his place and
got my things that I'd left there.

579
00:42:08,493 --> 00:42:11,691
That would have been the
night before he was killed?

580
00:42:11,863 --> 00:42:13,422
- Yes.
- Mm-hm.

581
00:42:14,532 --> 00:42:22,372
Uh, is this one of the articles you
removed from Slick's room that night?

582
00:42:23,341 --> 00:42:25,435
That's my hairbrush.

583
00:42:25,610 --> 00:42:27,078
How did you get it, Ben?

584
00:42:28,146 --> 00:42:29,580
I mean, Mr. Matlock.

585
00:42:29,747 --> 00:42:31,215
Armed with a search warrant,

586
00:42:31,382 --> 00:42:34,716
the police removed it from
your home earlier today.

587
00:42:34,886 --> 00:42:36,718
Now, when did you
take it from Slick's room?

588
00:42:37,288 --> 00:42:41,350
- I just said the night before he died.
- Mm-hm.

589
00:42:41,526 --> 00:42:44,121
We examined the strands
of hair that were in this brush.

590
00:42:44,295 --> 00:42:47,424
Some, of course, was your hair.

591
00:42:47,598 --> 00:42:51,330
But there were several
strands of darker hair

592
00:42:51,502 --> 00:42:52,936
matched that of decedent.

593
00:42:53,104 --> 00:42:55,335
That was Slick's hair.

594
00:42:55,673 --> 00:42:57,301
He lost his hairbrush.

595
00:42:57,475 --> 00:42:58,966
As a matter of
fact, he broke it,

596
00:42:59,610 --> 00:43:00,737
and he borrowed mine.

597
00:43:00,912 --> 00:43:03,643
You see, he was too
cheap to buy a new one.

598
00:43:03,815 --> 00:43:06,046
So what? MATLOCK: Guess what.

599
00:43:07,085 --> 00:43:12,490
Some of those strands of darker
hair were about 3 inches long

600
00:43:12,657 --> 00:43:16,526
and others were
about 1 inch long.

601
00:43:16,694 --> 00:43:20,392
I suppose that's because
Slick just got his hair cut.

602
00:43:20,565 --> 00:43:23,160
Here's a sworn
affidavit from his barber.

603
00:43:25,503 --> 00:43:26,783
I don't understand

604
00:43:26,938 --> 00:43:29,032
what any of this
has to do with me.

605
00:43:29,207 --> 00:43:33,135
His barber swears
that he cut Slick's hair

606
00:43:33,311 --> 00:43:36,645
at 10 a.m. the
day he was killed.

607
00:43:37,648 --> 00:43:38,928
And that means

608
00:43:39,016 --> 00:43:42,885
you could not have removed
your brush from Slick's room

609
00:43:43,054 --> 00:43:44,147
when you said you did.

610
00:43:44,322 --> 00:43:47,690
It had to be after
he got his hair cut.

611
00:43:47,859 --> 00:43:50,693
You took the brush after
you shot him, didn't you?

612
00:43:51,896 --> 00:43:55,060
- Ben.
- You and Slick were having an affair.

613
00:43:55,233 --> 00:43:57,225
Maybe you wanted to end it.

614
00:43:57,401 --> 00:43:59,802
Maybe you realized the
only way you could do that

615
00:43:59,971 --> 00:44:04,671
without jeopardizing your share of
your husband's considerable wealth

616
00:44:04,842 --> 00:44:05,866
was to kill Slick.

617
00:44:06,043 --> 00:44:07,067
Oh, Ben.

618
00:44:07,245 --> 00:44:11,615
So you stole your
husband's gun from his office,

619
00:44:11,782 --> 00:44:14,342
slipped out of the clinic
where you'd taken his mother,

620
00:44:14,519 --> 00:44:19,150
went over to the rooming house,
which was less than 10 minutes away.

621
00:44:19,323 --> 00:44:21,224
- Ben...
- Used the throw cushion

622
00:44:21,392 --> 00:44:24,624
from Slick's sofa to muffle
the sound, shot him to death.

623
00:44:24,795 --> 00:44:27,162
That's when you
took the hairbrush.

624
00:44:27,331 --> 00:44:28,890
Then you went downstairs,

625
00:44:29,066 --> 00:44:32,127
waited for Billy to show up,
thanks to the note you'd left him,

626
00:44:32,303 --> 00:44:33,343
then took the other gun...

627
00:44:33,504 --> 00:44:36,770
Ben, what I've been
trying to tell you is

628
00:44:37,041 --> 00:44:39,510
that's my nephew's hair.

629
00:44:45,483 --> 00:44:47,349
I beg your pardon?

630
00:44:47,518 --> 00:44:51,114
My nephew from
Raleigh is staying with me,

631
00:44:51,289 --> 00:44:55,420
and he forgot his brush
so he's been using mine.

632
00:44:55,593 --> 00:44:57,585
Jeff, darling, stand up

633
00:44:57,762 --> 00:45:00,527
so everybody can
see your precious hair.

634
00:45:12,677 --> 00:45:16,477
I don't... LEANNE:
What's wrong, Ben?

635
00:45:16,647 --> 00:45:18,639
This is your big moment

636
00:45:18,816 --> 00:45:22,082
to nail the killer on the stand.

637
00:45:26,691 --> 00:45:28,125
Oh, you poor darling.

638
00:45:28,626 --> 00:45:31,255
Everybody's laughing at you.

639
00:45:31,429 --> 00:45:33,455
You're making
a fool of yourself.

640
00:45:36,133 --> 00:45:37,965
I mean...

641
00:45:40,504 --> 00:45:42,268
Come on, Bennie.

642
00:45:42,440 --> 00:45:44,932
You didn't even
check the police lab.

643
00:45:46,711 --> 00:45:48,111
What's wrong?

644
00:45:48,879 --> 00:45:50,313
Hmm?

645
00:45:50,915 --> 00:45:52,679
What's wrong?

646
00:45:54,185 --> 00:45:55,983
What's wrong?

647
00:45:57,054 --> 00:45:58,818
Dad?

648
00:45:59,724 --> 00:46:02,250
I can't do it
anymore. It's over.

649
00:46:02,426 --> 00:46:04,418
Dad, what's wrong?

650
00:46:07,164 --> 00:46:08,894
Dad.

651
00:46:09,967 --> 00:46:11,629
Dad.

652
00:46:12,637 --> 00:46:14,299
Is it...?

653
00:46:16,107 --> 00:46:17,769
Is it you?

654
00:46:18,242 --> 00:46:20,643
Well, yes, it's me.

655
00:46:20,811 --> 00:46:23,110
You didn't do it.

656
00:46:23,281 --> 00:46:24,874
I didn't do what?

657
00:46:25,049 --> 00:46:27,644
Oh, sweetheart.

658
00:46:27,985 --> 00:46:30,853
I had this awful dream.

659
00:46:31,022 --> 00:46:32,615
- Oh.
- What are you doing down here?

660
00:46:32,790 --> 00:46:34,383
Why aren't you upstairs in bed?

661
00:46:34,558 --> 00:46:36,026
Well, I sat down.

662
00:46:36,193 --> 00:46:40,324
The histamine hit me
too hard to get that far.

663
00:46:42,933 --> 00:46:45,266
- Oh, Dad, you're hot.
- Oh, no, I'm fine.

664
00:46:45,436 --> 00:46:47,632
It's just that awful dream.

665
00:46:47,805 --> 00:46:49,535
I'm gonna get you
something cool to drink.

666
00:46:49,707 --> 00:46:51,507
- How about a nice glass of iced...?
- No. No.

667
00:46:51,609 --> 00:46:55,046
No, Leanne. No iced tea.

668
00:46:55,212 --> 00:46:57,238
Let's just have a...

669
00:46:58,749 --> 00:47:01,617
A couple glasses
of nice warm milk

670
00:47:03,321 --> 00:47:08,316
and sing "Stormy Weather."

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
